Live draw: INLINE_ARRAY vertices ignore the frequency divider. Vertex n of an inline stream reads element n; the RSX applies
no divider, modulo or base index to inline data (RPCS3 RSXDrawCommands.cpp analyse_inputs_interleaved: the inlined branch
registers every attribute with frequency 1, no modulo, and returns before frequency_divider_mask is read). A divider left in
an attribute's format word by an earlier array draw made every inline vertex read element vertex/f (or vertex%f): upstream
issue #457 item E1 (feanor-noldorin). Every fetch path: fetch_attr (rsx_live_draw.c), rsx_vertex_fetch_attr_one
(rsx_vertex_compact.c) and rsx_vertex_fetch_many's block loop. Host test:
port/rc/tests/run_inline_divider_test.sh (R&C).
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: rsx_vertex_fetch_many no longer falls back to the per-vertex fetch for a
divided attribute: KZ3 2040/2073's block loop (RSX_FETCH_LOOP) computes the element itself, with the divider. It gets
the same rule (inline: element = vertex_id); found by the host test, whose fetch_many cases read 0 0 0 0 1 1 1 1 without
it. The test's fetch_many call follows v0.18.0's signature (the stride is the plan's).

